    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d58">

                <pb facs="0076" n="70" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg70"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Goschen to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 59.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">New
                            London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1894-10-14"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 14, 1894</hi></date>. (Received
                        October 16.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I duly informed Her Majesty’s principal
                    secretary of state for foreign affairs of the reply of the United States
                    Government respecting the proposed intervention between China and Japan, which
                    you <pb facs="0077" n="71" xml:id="pg71"/> were good enough to communicate to me
                    by telegraph on the 12th instant.</p>
                <p>I am now instructed by his lordship to call your attention to the fact that the
                    intervention contemplated would be limited to diplomatic action and would only
                    take place in the event of a suitable opportunity presenting itself for the
                    adoption of such a course.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. E. Goschen.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
